# Undeclared user properties (issue #70). `:p` is never declared, so `:a :p :b`
# is an object property assertion or an annotation, and `:editorNote "..."` a
# data property assertion or an annotation; no position fixes either kind.
# HOWL does not guess: each property is one UndeclaredProperty omission citing
# its triples, the rest of the document is read (B subClassOf A is derived),
# and the run is INCONCLUSIVE (exit 2), not an input error (exit 3).

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class .
:B rdfs:subClassOf :A .
:a a owl:NamedIndividual . :b a owl:NamedIndividual .

:A :editorNote "needs review" .
:B :editorNote "split from A" .
:a :p :b .
